  "term": "ethosuximide",
  "definition": "Ethosuximide is an anticonvulsant succinimide that helps prevent seizures by stabilizing nerve activity in the brain. Its action is not fully understood, but it likely works in part by blocking T-type calcium channels in thalamic neurons and reducing burst firing in thalamocortical pathways.",
